# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings on every system, so the
# generated files this repository compares byte for byte read the same on
# Windows as on Linux and macOS. Git tells binaries by their content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The fonts' licence texts are copied verbatim from upstream, CRLF line endings
# included, and stay byte for byte as they were published.
assets/fonts/OFL-*.txt -text

# The packages that carry the faces hold copies of that directory, and
# `cargo xtask check` holds every copy to its source byte for byte: a licence
# normalised in the copy and not in the source would differ on a fresh clone.
crates/noctua-design-fonts*/fonts/** -text
packages/fonts/fonts/** -text

# The fuzzy corpus is another repository's file, held to a recorded checksum:
# it stays byte for byte as it was copied.
assets/vendor/nc-fuzzy/fuzzy-corpus.tsv -text
